   AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE SOURCE AND THIS MEASUREMENT (the layout was read off the bytes FIRST, in
   tools/bench/t2_rsrc_probe.log, and the search was answered afterwards -- they agree on all five):
     32-byte header, four u32 BE = info_offset / info_size / data_offset / data_size   ..... agree
     the 32-byte header is repeated at rsrc_info_offset                                 ..... agree
     BlockInfoListHeader = 5 u32; blockinfo_offset REL to rsrc_info_offset, value 52    ..... agree
     block count and per-block section count are both stored as (count - 1)             ..... agree
     BlockSectionStart is 20 BYTES; its 4th u32 is data_offset, REL to rsrc_data_offset ..... agree
     section payload carries a u32 length prefix, EXCLUSIVE of itself                   ..... agree
   The source adds one field name this measurement could not name: the 2nd u32 of BlockSectionStart
   is `name_offset` (0xFFFFFFFF = no name).  That matches the observed ff ff ff ff on 130 of 131
   records.  It also names the check this script's C7 already performs ("consecutive sections tile
   the data region with only 0-3 padding bytes between them").

