E. CAVEAT THE SEARCH RAISED, recorded because it bounds what the tables above mean
   Since LabVIEW 8.0 some sections are ZLIB-COMPRESSED INSIDE the section (the heap blocks and VICD
   among them).  This script hashes the STORED bytes of each section, which is the right measurement
   for "what did the save rewrite on disk".  It follows that an identical sha256 proves the stored
   bytes are identical, while a DIFFERING sha256 does not by itself separate a content change from a
   recompression.  Neither case is interpreted here.  The search also warns its own knowledge stops
   around LabVIEW 2014-2020 and that no public reverse-engineering of LabVIEW 2026 was found; the
   self-checks C1-C7 are what stand behind these tables for this pair of files.

